# Reference:
#   https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Purpose:
#   Automatically assigns reviewers to every Pull Request based on
#   the files being modified. GitHub triggers these reviewers
#   automatically when a PR is opened.
#
# Syntax:
#   <pattern>    <owner1> <owner2> ...
#
# Supported patterns:
#   *           → all files (fallback)
#   /proxy/     → a specific directory
#   /docs/*.md  → specific files (glob)
#   *.go        → all Go files (extension glob)
#
# Matching rules:
#   • The last matching pattern wins (more specific overrides
#     more general).
#   • Order matters: general first, then specific.
#   • Blank lines are for readability only.
#   • Comments must be on their own line (starting with #).
#
# ⚠️ Note:
#   CODEOWNERS works on FILE PATHS only — it does NOT control
#   branch rules. For branch policies (which branches can be
#   pushed to, PR targets, etc.), see:
#     • docs/BRANCHING.md §6 (Branch Protection)
#     • Repository Settings → Branches
#     • Repository Settings → Rules → Rulesets
